1
00:00:08,940 --> 00:00:10,400
Water Demon.

2
00:00:12,060 --> 00:00:13,880
Ice Dragon.

3
00:00:14,630 --> 00:00:17,420
Lesser Warlord of Ka'a.

4
00:00:17,420 --> 00:00:19,610
Not so fast.

5
00:00:20,490 --> 00:00:22,470
Infinite Sheldon.

6
00:00:24,130 --> 00:00:25,380
Infinite Sheldon?

7
00:00:25,380 --> 00:00:28,370
Yes, Infinite Sheldon defeats all other cards

8
00:00:28,370 --> 00:00:30,640
and does not violate the rule against homemade cards

9
00:00:30,640 --> 00:00:33,000
because I made it at work.

10
00:00:34,850 --> 00:00:37,640
Do you understand why people don't want to play with you?

11
00:00:37,640 --> 00:00:38,980
No...

12
00:00:38,980 --> 00:00:42,180
Although it's a question I've been pondering since preschool.

13
00:00:47,570 --> 00:00:49,910
Hey, your copy of Science Magazine was in my mailbox.

14
00:00:49,910 --> 00:00:51,050
Oh, thanks. Mm-hmm.

15
00:00:51,050 --> 00:00:53,750
Check it out, all about planets this month.

16
00:00:54,180 --> 00:00:55,770
That's an atom.

17
00:00:56,890 --> 00:00:58,800
Agree to disagree.

18
00:00:59,810 --> 00:01:01,350
That's what I love about science.

19
00:01:01,350 --> 00:01:03,420
There's no one right answer.

20
00:01:08,270 --> 00:01:09,430
So...

21
00:01:09,430 --> 00:01:10,600
You and Zack again, huh?

22
00:01:10,600 --> 00:01:12,750
Yeah, yeah, me and Zack again.

23
00:01:12,750 --> 00:01:14,810
Were we here earlier?

24
00:01:16,360 --> 00:01:17,480
Okay, we should, we should go.

25
00:01:17,480 --> 00:01:18,350
Ah, not yet.

26
00:01:18,350 --> 00:01:20,540
I want to talk science with the science dudes.

27
00:01:20,540 --> 00:01:24,840
Oh, and the science dudes want to talk science with you.

28
00:01:25,610 --> 00:01:26,680
What do you want to talk about,

29
00:01:26,680 --> 00:01:30,600
rocks, dinosaurs, our friend the beaver?

30
00:01:31,890 --> 00:01:34,440
You know, I saw this great thing on the Discovery Channel.

31
00:01:34,440 --> 00:01:36,590
Turns out that if you kill a starfish,

32
00:01:36,590 --> 00:01:38,500
it'll just come back to life.

33
00:01:40,350 --> 00:01:42,190
Was the starfish wearing boxer shorts?

34
00:01:42,190 --> 00:01:44,960
Because you might have been watching Nickelodeon.

35
00:01:47,460 --> 00:01:51,390
No, I'm almost sure that it was the Discovery Channel.

36
00:01:51,390 --> 00:01:52,060
It was a great show.

37
00:01:52,060 --> 00:01:54,850
They also said dolphins might be smarter than people.

38
00:01:55,200 --> 00:01:57,990
They might be smarter than some people.

39
00:02:00,130 --> 00:02:02,540
Maybe we can do an experiment to find out.

40
00:02:02,540 --> 00:02:03,840
That's easy enough.

41
00:02:03,840 --> 00:02:07,090
We'd need a large tank of water, a hoop to jump through,

42
00:02:07,090 --> 00:02:11,470
and a bucket of whatever bite-sized treats you find tasty.

43
00:02:17,900 --> 00:02:19,520
I don't get it.

44
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:21,930
A dolphin might.

45
00:02:25,590 --> 00:02:26,150
Oh, I see.

46
00:02:26,150 --> 00:02:27,790
You guys are inferring that I'm stupid.

47
00:02:27,790 --> 00:02:29,350
That's not correct.

48
00:02:29,350 --> 00:02:31,720
We were implying it.

49
00:02:32,840 --> 00:02:35,250
You then inferred it.

50
00:02:38,470 --> 00:02:39,990
Let's go.

51
00:02:42,440 --> 00:02:43,680
You know, for a group of guys

52
00:02:43,680 --> 00:02:46,250
who claim they spent most of their lives being bullied,

53
00:02:46,250 --> 00:02:47,790
you can be real jerks.

54
00:02:47,790 --> 00:02:49,690
Shame on all of you.

55
00:02:52,370 --> 00:02:54,390
What the hell did I do?

56
00:02:55,450 --> 00:02:57,150
You laughed.

57
00:03:24,190 --> 00:03:25,260
Do you think Penny's right?

58
00:03:25,260 --> 00:03:27,000
Were we bullying Zack?

59
00:03:27,000 --> 00:03:28,730
No, I know bullying.

60
00:03:28,730 --> 00:03:32,460
He left here unswirlied and his ass crack was underpants-free.

61
00:03:34,010 --> 00:03:36,710
And nobody drew a penis on his forehead.

62
00:03:39,090 --> 00:03:40,790
That happened to you?

63
00:03:41,280 --> 00:03:43,130
First day of cricket camp.

64
00:03:43,130 --> 00:03:45,920
They drew it so the testicles were my eyes.

65
00:03:49,790 --> 00:03:52,300
I don't know, I think we might owe the guy an apology.

66
00:03:52,300 --> 00:03:54,850
- So go apologize. - Why me?

67
00:03:54,850 --> 00:03:57,490
You started it, we just piled on.

68
00:03:58,610 --> 00:03:59,830
What would I even say?

69
00:03:59,830 --> 00:04:02,630
Zack, I'm sorry you're stupid.

70
00:04:05,300 --> 00:04:07,250
Have a Milk Dud.

71
00:04:08,520 --> 00:04:09,560
A Milk Dud?

72
00:04:09,560 --> 00:04:12,260
Yeah, Milk Duds, with their self-deprecating name

73
00:04:12,260 --> 00:04:14,130
and remarkably mild flavor,

74
00:04:14,130 --> 00:04:17,260
are the most apologetic of the boxed candies.

75
00:04:18,730 --> 00:04:19,630
I got a better idea.

76
00:04:19,630 --> 00:04:20,480
We're all responsible.

77
00:04:20,480 --> 00:04:22,050
I say we all go.

78
00:04:25,100 --> 00:04:27,160
Come on, who's with me?

79
00:04:28,530 --> 00:04:31,730
Free comic books to anyone who comes with me.

80
00:04:32,960 --> 00:04:35,500
I might get punched. You really want to miss that?

81
00:04:40,960 --> 00:04:42,700
Junior Mints are pretty apologetic.

82
00:04:42,700 --> 00:04:44,800
You're embarrassing yourself.

83
00:04:49,180 --> 00:04:50,720
Penny.

84
00:04:56,090 --> 00:04:59,190
- What? - Yeah, we came to talk to Zack. Hey, Zack.

85
00:04:59,190 --> 00:05:00,520
What do you want?

86
00:05:00,520 --> 00:05:02,130
Listen, the stuff we were saying before,

87
00:05:02,130 --> 00:05:03,850
we were just kidding around.

88
00:05:03,850 --> 00:05:04,580
No, you weren't.

89
00:05:04,580 --> 00:05:06,140
You were making fun of me.

90
00:05:06,470 --> 00:05:08,000
Come on, that's what we do.

91
00:05:08,000 --> 00:05:10,340
We give each other a hard time.

92
00:05:10,340 --> 00:05:11,260
Hey, Sheldon,

93
00:05:11,260 --> 00:05:13,400
you look like a praying mantis.

94
00:05:15,720 --> 00:05:16,670
That's very hurtful.

95
00:05:16,670 --> 00:05:18,260
See?

96
00:05:19,500 --> 00:05:22,090
I don't know, it still wasn't very nice.

97
00:05:22,090 --> 00:05:24,190
Milk Dud?

98
00:05:24,190 --> 00:05:25,830
Oh, I love Milk Duds.

99
00:05:27,420 --> 00:05:29,170
Okay, we're cool.

100
00:05:31,160 --> 00:05:33,860
Junior Mints.

101
00:05:34,440 --> 00:05:35,690
You guys want to come in and have a beer?

102
00:05:35,690 --> 00:05:37,470
Uh, we're on our way to the comic book store.

103
00:05:37,470 --> 00:05:39,080
Leonard's buying.

104
00:05:39,080 --> 00:05:39,950
Really?

105
00:05:39,950 --> 00:05:41,160
I haven't been to a comic book store

106
00:05:41,160 --> 00:05:43,360
in literally a million years.

107
00:05:43,740 --> 00:05:44,800
Literally?

108
00:05:44,800 --> 00:05:47,600
Literally a million years?

109
00:05:48,260 --> 00:05:49,480
Don't.

110
00:05:49,480 --> 00:05:50,980
- You want to go with 'em?  - No.

111
00:05:50,980 --> 00:05:52,240
- Okay, see you later.  - Wait,

112
00:05:52,240 --> 00:05:56,990
w-w-w-wait, you're ditching me to go look at comic books?

113
00:05:56,990 --> 00:05:58,400
Are you mad at me?

114
00:05:58,400 --> 00:06:00,280
I'm not happy.

115
00:06:02,400 --> 00:06:04,050
Milk Dud?

116
00:06:08,010 --> 00:06:10,230
Wow, this place is awesome.

117
00:06:10,230 --> 00:06:12,140
Where do they keep the Archies?

118
00:06:12,850 --> 00:06:16,540
In the bedrooms of ten-year-old girls, where they belong.

119
00:06:16,800 --> 00:06:18,490
Oh, no, you're thinking old-school Archie.

120
00:06:18,490 --> 00:06:20,250
It's much more sophisticated now.

121
00:06:20,250 --> 00:06:21,780
Like, there's two universes,

122
00:06:21,780 --> 00:06:23,270
and Archie's married to Betty in one

123
00:06:23,270 --> 00:06:24,580
and Veronica in the other.

124
00:06:24,580 --> 00:06:26,860
Midge is even breaking up with Moose.

125
00:06:26,860 --> 00:06:28,470
No.

126
00:06:29,000 --> 00:06:30,540
About time, right?

127
00:06:31,220 --> 00:06:34,980
Hey. You guys finally chip in for a bodyguard?

128
00:06:36,660 --> 00:06:38,140
Uh, no. Oh, this is Zack.

129
00:06:38,140 --> 00:06:40,110
He's a friend of ours.

130
00:06:40,110 --> 00:06:41,050
Zack, this is Stuart.

131
00:06:41,050 --> 00:06:42,310
He owns the store.

132
00:06:42,310 --> 00:06:44,100
Wow, lucky you.

133
00:06:44,100 --> 00:06:46,750
Yeah, I work 70 hours a week

134
00:06:46,750 --> 00:06:49,920
and average $1.65 an hour.

135
00:06:50,350 --> 00:06:52,210
Sweet.

136
00:06:53,620 --> 00:06:55,180
Is that sarcasm?

137
00:06:55,180 --> 00:06:59,210
No, it's an indictment of the American education system.

138
00:07:00,070 --> 00:07:01,630
The Archies are over here.

139
00:07:01,630 --> 00:07:03,360
Yippee.

140
00:07:05,110 --> 00:07:07,940
So are you guys coming to my New Year's Eve costume party?

141
00:07:07,940 --> 00:07:08,850
Of course.

142
00:07:08,850 --> 00:07:11,090
We're coming as the Justice League of America.

143
00:07:11,090 --> 00:07:12,340
Switching it up from last year

144
00:07:12,340 --> 00:07:15,480
when we came as the Justice League of America.

145
00:07:16,200 --> 00:07:17,310
To that point,

146
00:07:17,310 --> 00:07:20,360
it occurs to me that we might have an opportunity

147
00:07:20,360 --> 00:07:22,970
to finally snare Best Group Costume

148
00:07:22,970 --> 00:07:25,060
if we shore up our weak link,

149
00:07:25,060 --> 00:07:28,060
which is clearly Leonard as Superman.

150
00:07:29,280 --> 00:07:31,020
Hey, I got new boots this year.

151
00:07:31,020 --> 00:07:33,450
Guaranteed to add three inches.

152
00:07:34,300 --> 00:07:36,120
That's sad.

153
00:07:37,530 --> 00:07:39,000
Let's ask ourselves:

154
00:07:39,000 --> 00:07:41,210
Is there anyone we know

155
00:07:41,210 --> 00:07:45,990
who would make a more manly and convincing son of Krypton?

156
00:07:45,990 --> 00:07:48,880
Than Leonard in high-heeled boots?

157
00:07:49,700 --> 00:07:52,450
Howard's mother in high-heeled boots?

158
00:07:55,060 --> 00:07:58,650
I was thinking specifically of the gentleman over there

159
00:07:58,650 --> 00:08:03,470
moving his lips as he enjoys the latest exploits of Betty and Veronica.

160
00:08:06,870 --> 00:08:08,350
Zack?

161
00:08:08,350 --> 00:08:12,670
He is the only person we know with actual muscles.

162
00:08:12,670 --> 00:08:15,010
You can't replace me with Zack.

163
00:08:15,010 --> 00:08:17,350
Why not? Penny did it.

164
00:08:18,310 --> 00:08:19,630
Yeah, she seems happier.

165
00:08:19,630 --> 00:08:21,550
Why wouldn't we be?

166
00:08:22,160 --> 00:08:22,920
Score.

167
00:08:22,920 --> 00:08:25,020
I got an Archie, Betty and Veronica,

168
00:08:25,020 --> 00:08:26,180
and a Jughead.

169
00:08:26,180 --> 00:08:28,710
All set for my weekend number twos.

170
00:08:30,190 --> 00:08:31,970
Congratulations.

171
00:08:31,970 --> 00:08:36,340
Zack, how would you like to be Superman?

172
00:08:36,340 --> 00:08:39,450
I don't kow. Sounds like a lot of responsibility.

173
00:08:43,340 --> 00:08:44,990
Fine. If Zack's gonna be Superman,

174
00:08:44,990 --> 00:08:46,290
I want to be Green Lantern.

175
00:08:46,290 --> 00:08:47,330
But I'm Green Lantern.

176
00:08:47,330 --> 00:08:48,790
You can be Aquaman.

177
00:08:48,790 --> 00:08:49,900
I don't want to be Aquaman.

178
00:08:49,900 --> 00:08:51,990
He sucks.

179
00:08:53,170 --> 00:08:55,870
He sucks underwater.

180
00:08:56,570 --> 00:08:58,830
He sucks fish pee.

181
00:08:59,440 --> 00:09:00,620
Excuse me,

182
00:09:00,620 --> 00:09:03,940
I believe Aquaman uses his telepathic powers

183
00:09:03,940 --> 00:09:07,470
to request the fish do their business elsewhere.

184
00:09:08,660 --> 00:09:09,360
Hey, babe.

185
00:09:09,360 --> 00:09:10,680
I'm still mad at you.

186
00:09:10,680 --> 00:09:12,840
Well, you won't be when you hear the great news.

187
00:09:12,840 --> 00:09:14,070
What great news?

188
00:09:14,070 --> 00:09:15,490
We're going to a costume party

189
00:09:15,490 --> 00:09:18,120
at the comic book store on New Year's Eve,

190
00:09:18,120 --> 00:09:20,430
and you get to be Wonder Woman.

191
00:09:21,830 --> 00:09:25,360
Complete with bulletproof bracelets and lasso of truth.

192
00:09:25,820 --> 00:09:28,130
Invisible plane sold separately.

193
00:09:29,080 --> 00:09:30,240
Wait, why me?

194
00:09:30,240 --> 00:09:32,370
Wh-Why can't your girlfriend be Wonder Woman?

195
00:09:32,370 --> 00:09:35,100
She and her lab team are under quarantine.

196
00:09:35,100 --> 00:09:37,850
Seems at the Christmas party they were doing Jell-O shots

197
00:09:37,850 --> 00:09:41,620
out of petri dishes that used to contain yellow fever.

198
00:09:42,810 --> 00:09:45,770
Okay, what about your friend Amy?

199
00:09:45,770 --> 00:09:48,750
Amy Farrah Fowler doesn't believe in wearing costumes.

200
00:09:48,750 --> 00:09:51,550
She isn't the free spirit I am.

201
00:09:54,730 --> 00:09:55,660
Okay, well, forget it.

202
00:09:55,660 --> 00:09:56,980
I'm not spending my New Year's Eve

203
00:09:56,980 --> 00:10:00,170
at a comic book store wearing a Wonder Woman costume.

204
00:10:01,780 --> 00:10:05,560
He says he'll wear it if you'll be Aquaman.

205
00:10:19,590 --> 00:10:21,210
What are you doing?

206
00:10:21,620 --> 00:10:22,890
We're going to be late.

207
00:10:22,890 --> 00:10:24,820
I'm pacing nervously.

208
00:10:25,580 --> 00:10:27,190
You're jogging.

209
00:10:27,190 --> 00:10:29,340
This is how the Flash paces.

210
00:10:30,600 --> 00:10:32,140
Just chill out, Sheldon.

211
00:10:32,140 --> 00:10:35,040
I'm not Sheldon. I'm the Flash.

212
00:10:35,560 --> 00:10:37,000
And now I'm going to the Grand Canyon

213
00:10:37,000 --> 00:10:39,110
to scream in frustration.

214
00:10:39,110 --> 00:10:40,800
I'm back.

215
00:10:43,930 --> 00:10:46,090
I'm Batman.

216
00:10:47,250 --> 00:10:48,660
Oh, I hardly think so.

217
00:10:48,660 --> 00:10:51,300
The real caped crusader calls his crime-fighting cohorts

218
00:10:51,300 --> 00:10:53,250
when he's running late.

219
00:10:53,990 --> 00:10:54,730
I had to walk.

220
00:10:54,730 --> 00:10:57,550
I couldn't get Raj on the back of my scooter.

221
00:11:05,340 --> 00:11:07,570
I've said this before, and I'll say it again.

222
00:11:07,570 --> 00:11:10,060
Aquaman sucks.

223
00:11:10,060 --> 00:11:13,690
Look up in the sky. It's a bird. It's a plane.

224
00:11:15,550 --> 00:11:17,310
I forget the rest.

225
00:11:18,780 --> 00:11:21,140
All right. Let's get this thing over with.

226
00:11:23,200 --> 00:11:24,420
I'm sorry.

227
00:11:24,420 --> 00:11:28,110
But in what universe is Wonder Woman blonde?

228
00:11:28,110 --> 00:11:30,990
Relax. No one's going to be looking at her hair.

229
00:11:33,240 --> 00:11:34,750
Ow!

230
00:11:36,770 --> 00:11:37,340
I mean,

231
00:11:37,340 --> 00:11:39,090
ow.

232
00:11:40,660 --> 00:11:42,970
Hold on. The costume came with a black wig. Where is it, babe?

233
00:11:42,970 --> 00:11:44,870
No. I'm not wearing it. It looks stupid.

234
00:11:44,870 --> 00:11:46,570
Come on. We're trying to win a contest here.

235
00:11:46,570 --> 00:11:48,210
Forget it. I'm not wearing the wig.

236
00:11:48,210 --> 00:11:51,840
Penny, there's no "I" In "Justice League."

237
00:11:54,730 --> 00:11:55,920
Well, actually...

238
00:11:55,920 --> 00:11:59,110
Don't. He's making our case.

239
00:11:59,870 --> 00:12:00,730
Okay, babe. Uh...

240
00:12:00,730 --> 00:12:03,500
Kind of embarrassing me in front of my friends.

241
00:12:04,710 --> 00:12:05,640
Okay. You know what?

242
00:12:05,640 --> 00:12:08,370
I changed my mind. I'm not going.

243
00:12:10,010 --> 00:12:13,870
Looks like someone else is going to have to be Wonder Woman.

244
00:12:18,430 --> 00:12:20,180
Babe, open up.

245
00:12:20,180 --> 00:12:22,190
I'm not talking to you.

246
00:12:22,190 --> 00:12:24,470
Then who are you talking to?

247
00:12:27,680 --> 00:12:29,540
Babe?

248
00:12:29,820 --> 00:12:37,660
Penny, Penny, Penny, Penny, Penny, Penny, Penny,

249
00:12:38,150 --> 00:12:40,590
What the hell is wrong with you?

250
00:12:41,140 --> 00:12:41,970
I'm the Flash.

251
00:12:41,970 --> 00:12:44,410
I just knocked 30,000 times.

252
00:12:44,860 --> 00:12:46,390
Okay. What do you want, Sheldon?

253
00:12:46,390 --> 00:12:49,360
I understand why you're upset.

254
00:12:49,360 --> 00:12:50,350
Really?

255
00:12:50,350 --> 00:12:51,480
Yes.

256
00:12:51,480 --> 00:12:54,810
You're afraid that costume makes you look fat.

257
00:12:57,170 --> 00:12:58,470
No.

258
00:12:58,470 --> 00:12:59,850
Wh-What...

259
00:12:59,850 --> 00:13:01,160
Does it?

260
00:13:02,000 --> 00:13:03,210
Don't worry.

261
00:13:03,210 --> 00:13:05,500
Wonder Woman was an Amazon.

262
00:13:05,500 --> 00:13:09,340
And Amazons tend to be very beefy gals.

263
00:13:11,490 --> 00:13:13,500
Good-bye, Sheldon.

264
00:13:15,810 --> 00:13:19,780
But they're not blonde, so put on your wig.

265
00:13:22,430 --> 00:13:24,060
Hello?

266
00:13:34,660 --> 00:13:37,100
Stupid Aquaman.

267
00:13:38,930 --> 00:13:40,470
If it makes you feel any better,

268
00:13:40,470 --> 00:13:41,440
when I was dating Penny,

269
00:13:41,440 --> 00:13:43,960
she used to flip out on me all the time.

270
00:13:43,960 --> 00:13:46,300
Whoa. You dated Penny?

271
00:13:47,660 --> 00:13:49,250
She didn't tell you?

272
00:13:49,250 --> 00:13:51,150
She told me she dated a guy named Leonard.

273
00:13:51,150 --> 00:13:53,360
Who would have thought it was you?

274
00:13:54,440 --> 00:13:56,370
Who else would it be?

275
00:13:56,370 --> 00:13:59,420
I don't know. Somebody bigger and...

276
00:13:59,420 --> 00:14:02,030
Yeah, sure. Why not you?

277
00:14:05,080 --> 00:14:07,170
I may have failed.

278
00:14:07,620 --> 00:14:10,690
Okay, I guess we just go without a Wonder Woman.

279
00:14:10,690 --> 00:14:12,210
I don't want to go without Penny.

280
00:14:12,210 --> 00:14:16,010
Oh, great. No Superman, no Wonder Woman?

281
00:14:16,010 --> 00:14:17,540
All we've got is a skinny Flash,

282
00:14:17,540 --> 00:14:19,020
an Indian Aquaman,

283
00:14:19,020 --> 00:14:20,550
a nearsighted Green Lantern,

284
00:14:20,550 --> 00:14:23,380
and a teeny, tiny Dark Knight.

285
00:14:25,540 --> 00:14:28,390
Obviously, we're no longer a Justice League.

286
00:14:28,390 --> 00:14:32,460
We have no choice but to switch to our Muppet Baby costumes.

287
00:14:34,380 --> 00:14:36,480
Ooh, I call Kermit.

288
00:14:36,480 --> 00:14:38,780
I'm Kermit. U're Scooter.

289
00:14:38,780 --> 00:14:41,340
Oh, man. Scooter sucks.

290
00:14:42,650 --> 00:14:45,260
He's the Aquaman of the Muppet Babies.

291
00:14:47,070 --> 00:14:49,380
No, we can still make this work.

292
00:14:49,380 --> 00:14:51,240
Leonard, you talk to Penny.

293
00:14:51,240 --> 00:14:53,220
What makes you think I can convince her?

294
00:14:53,220 --> 00:14:54,790
You got her to have sex with you.

295
00:14:54,790 --> 00:14:58,290
Obviously, your superpower is brainwashing.

296
00:15:00,970 --> 00:15:03,800
Okay, let me see if I understand this.

297
00:15:03,800 --> 00:15:06,140
You want me to convince my ex-girlfriend

298
00:15:06,140 --> 00:15:08,730
to go to a costume party with her new boyfriend

299
00:15:08,730 --> 00:15:10,730
just so we can win a stupid prize?

300
00:15:10,730 --> 00:15:13,700
Yes. And make her wear the black wig. Good luck.

301
00:15:16,380 --> 00:15:17,930
Go away, Sheldon.

302
00:15:17,930 --> 00:15:19,140
It's Leonard.

303
00:15:20,040 --> 00:15:22,100
Go away, Leonard.

304
00:15:22,990 --> 00:15:25,240
Come on, let me just talk to you.

305
00:15:25,710 --> 00:15:27,350
It's open.

306
00:15:28,970 --> 00:15:30,190
I'm not going to that party, Leonard.

307
00:15:30,190 --> 00:15:33,230
Okay, listen. You don't have to wear the wig.

308
00:15:33,230 --> 00:15:34,720
At this party, we're gonna win first prize

309
00:15:34,720 --> 00:15:37,170
just by showing up with a girl.

310
00:15:38,610 --> 00:15:40,320
It's not the wig.

311
00:15:40,320 --> 00:15:41,910
Did I do something?

312
00:15:41,910 --> 00:15:43,590
I mean, I tried to be friends with Zack,

313
00:15:43,590 --> 00:15:46,420
like you said, which believe me, was difficult,

314
00:15:46,420 --> 00:15:48,360
given how you and me used to be...

315
00:15:48,360 --> 00:15:52,830
you know, "You and me," And now you and him are "You and him."

316
00:15:53,500 --> 00:15:56,480
Okay, look. We're not really "Me and him."

317
00:15:56,480 --> 00:15:57,790
Then what are you?

318
00:15:58,290 --> 00:15:59,730
I don't know.

319
00:15:59,730 --> 00:16:01,440
I only started seeing Zack again

320
00:16:01,440 --> 00:16:04,230
so I wouldn't be alone on New Year's Eve.

321
00:16:04,450 --> 00:16:06,240
How pathetic is that?

322
00:16:06,240 --> 00:16:08,260
Not as pathetic as dressing up like this

323
00:16:08,260 --> 00:16:11,600
and going to a comic book store on New Year's Eve.

324
00:16:12,220 --> 00:16:14,780
You make a cute Green Arrow.

325
00:16:19,720 --> 00:16:21,630
Green Lantern.

326
00:16:22,290 --> 00:16:24,340
Like there's a difference.

327
00:16:24,910 --> 00:16:26,580
There's a big difference.

328
00:16:26,580 --> 00:16:28,330
Arrow.

329
00:16:28,330 --> 00:16:30,100
Lantern.

330
00:16:33,150 --> 00:16:34,930
Whatever. Look, if Zack and I had just gone

331
00:16:34,930 --> 00:16:37,660
to a regular club or a party, it would have been fine,

332
00:16:37,660 --> 00:16:39,740
but this, with the costumes, and you...

333
00:16:39,740 --> 00:16:41,380
What about me?

334
00:16:44,740 --> 00:16:45,880
Nothing.

335
00:16:45,880 --> 00:16:47,400
Let's go to the party.

336
00:16:49,480 --> 00:16:51,130
How do I look?

337
00:16:57,570 --> 00:17:00,250
I guarantee you'll be the prettiest girl there.

338
00:17:01,870 --> 00:17:04,290
Okay, the good news is, we have a Wonder Woman.

339
00:17:04,290 --> 00:17:05,300
Oh. Yes.

340
00:17:05,300 --> 00:17:06,520
What's the bad news?

341
00:17:06,520 --> 00:17:09,820
Superman probably isn't getting laid tonight.

342
00:17:11,700 --> 00:17:13,630
Aw, damn.

343
00:17:16,080 --> 00:17:20,980
And the award for best group costume goes to...

344
00:17:21,600 --> 00:17:23,940
Justice League of America...

345
00:17:29,260 --> 00:17:30,680
Number Three!

346
00:17:33,410 --> 00:17:36,490
Thank you! Thank you so much!

347
00:17:36,490 --> 00:17:39,410
Okay. Okay, ten seconds to midnight.

348
00:17:39,410 --> 00:17:40,950
Ten, nine, eight...

349
00:17:40,950 --> 00:17:42,020
No, wait!

350
00:17:42,020 --> 00:17:43,530
I have a speech.

351
00:17:43,530 --> 00:17:45,490
- Seven, six... - Stop counting!

352
00:17:45,490 --> 00:17:47,840
- Five, four, three... - This is my moment, dag nab it!

353
00:17:47,840 --> 00:17:49,280
Two, one!

354
00:17:49,280 --> 00:17:51,910
Happy New Year!

355
00:18:04,190 --> 00:18:06,120
I'm not going to say another word

356
00:18:06,120 --> 00:18:08,540
until you people settle down.

357
00:18:11,620 --> 00:18:13,320
I'm waiting.

358
00:18:16,930 --> 00:18:19,440
That was a great party.

359
00:18:19,440 --> 00:18:21,620
We should dress like this all the time.

360
00:18:22,610 --> 00:18:24,240
Are you high?

361
00:18:24,480 --> 00:18:26,470
You're being a bully.

362
00:18:30,330 --> 00:18:31,020
Check it out.

363
00:18:31,020 --> 00:18:33,400
Those guys are breaking into that car.

364
00:18:33,400 --> 00:18:34,890
What should we do?

365
00:18:35,160 --> 00:18:37,320
We're the Justice League of America.

366
00:18:37,320 --> 00:18:39,690
There's only one thing we can do.

367
00:18:39,690 --> 00:18:42,830
Turn around and slowly walk away.

368
00:18:50,530 --> 00:18:52,070
Nah.

369
00:18:52,710 --> 00:18:54,350
Hold up.

370
00:19:00,140 --> 00:19:02,190
Look, I know our winter thermostat setting

371
00:19:02,190 --> 00:19:03,970
is 72 degrees, but I'm a little warm,

372
00:19:03,970 --> 00:19:05,900
so I'm going to turn it down.

373
00:19:30,300 --> 00:19:35,890
Good Lord, how you frustrate me, Leonard Hofstadter!

374
00:19:53,670 --> 00:19:55,240
Fine.

